  "title": "Reading the tree back on fresh spaces",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Ticket B's rules and reconstruction hold on fresh spaces, except its glue rule. On 111 fresh spaces (all 100 three-fold classes of 23 to 26 points and 11 new trees of Fano atoms), creation computed exactly: all 32,016 fresh pairs of atom lines at B's 21 places have the relation B recorded there, and 6 places B never saw (zigzags) each carry one relation; all 163 cuts between two atoms read one way, from the receiver's intact lines to the emitter; and the source rule counts the Heawood braces, and the genus, on all 110 fresh spaces without a non-Fano brace (the plain block count on 83), failing only on the space built on census 58. B's glue prediction is refuted as stated: in one class (twisted 26-point class 65), 12 of the 24 pairs of glue lines with a Fano atom between them create, one way. With no handle between, glue lines are silent in all 1,354 fresh pairs, as in all 306 of B's.",
